{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Exercise Replace: Session vs Remaining Weeks",
  "description": "How picking a replacement exercise flows from Setcard to the scope dialog, and how the remaining-weeks scope is persisted and kept in sync with saved drafts.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "directory": "frontend",
      "title": "Frontend Layout",
      "description": "Pages hold route-level screens, components hold cards and dialogs, helper holds data shaping. The replace feature lives in pages/WorkoutUi.tsx (state + dialog) and components/setComponent.tsx (picker)."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 290,
      "title": "All Weeks Loaded Up Front",
      "description": "fetchAllweekdata pulls the whole mesocycle tree once per mesocycleId, and again silently after a replace. Every session, sessionexercise and set arrives together, which is why the client can compute the remaining-scope draft keys without another request."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 324,
      "title": "Current Session and Storage Key",
      "description": "The URL weeknumber/daynumber select one session out of data.sessions. storageKey scopes the local draft per day, so edits on one day do not leak into another day's draft."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/helper/copySessiondata.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Isolated Working Copy",
      "description": "copySessionData deep-copies sessionexercise and set and resets feedback. sessionData is the editable draft; data stays the untouched server snapshot. The remaining-weeks logic edits data through setData, never by mutating it."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 341,
      "title": "Saved Draft Wins",
      "description": "On mount, a localStorage draft for this day overrides the server copy. Gotcha: merely visiting a future day creates a draft, so a server-side replace alone would still be hidden by that older draft. This is why the remaining-weeks path removes the drafts it invalidates."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/components/setComponent.tsx",
      "line": 135,
      "title": "Picker Hands Off the Exercise",
      "description": "Selecting an exercise calls replaceExercise(exerciseData.exerciseId, exercise). The first argument is the global exercise ID, not the sessionexercise row ID, so every matching row can be found by exerciseId. The picker only offers exercises from the same muscle group."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 186,
      "title": "Replace Request Opens the Scope Dialog",
      "description": "replaceExercise does no mutation; it stores { oldId, newExercise } in replacePrompt, which renders the dialog. Both scopes start from this single entry point."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 466,
      "title": "The Remaining Week Button",
      "description": "This button calls replaceTheRemainingWeek. Its sibling below calls replaceForThisSession. The dialog text promises the remaining week, while the backend actually covers every pending session from this day to the end of the mesocycle."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 191,
      "title": "Session-Only Replace",
      "description": "replaceForThisSession swaps exerciseId and exercise, keeps the set count, blanks weight/reps/rir and resets status on the in-memory draft. Only localStorage persists it until the workout is completed."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 217,
      "title": "Remaining-Weeks Replace",
      "description": "Posts the swap to /training/replace, then applies the same swap locally for this session, clears drafts of pending later days, and silently refetches so other weeks show the new exercise. Note the server count is not used to report which days changed; the toast uses the server message."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/src/helper/replaceExercise.ts",
      "line": 4,
      "title": "The Scope Predicate",
      "description": "A single updateMany rewrites sessionexercise.exerciseId for every row where the exercise matches and the owning session is pending and is at or after the current week/day. Changing this filter is the only place that changes which weeks are covered; today is included via gte."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/src/route/Exercise.ts",
      "line": 15,
      "title": "Route Wiring",
      "description": "POST /api/training/replace reads the ids from the body, coerces them with Number, returns updated.count, and maps thrown errors to 400. Missing fields become NaN and fail in Prisma rather than being rejected explicitly."
    },
    {
      "title": "Next Move",
      "description": "The flow is complete end to end: picker, scope dialog, session draft, server write, draft invalidation, silent refresh. To widen or narrow the scope, edit the OR filter in backend/src/helper/replaceExercise.ts."
    }
  ]
}
